# interplay_memlive_inflight_rewrite: Five execs rung in one doorbell fill a live shared buffer and a live private buffer (the private one with invalidateGuest and synchronize, 6, so each is written back) at five offsets; right after the doorbell, without waiting, the guest points both leaves at other pages and writes those. Whenever each exec runs against the rewrite, its objects are already bound: every fill and every write-back lands in the old pages, and the new pages keep the guest's bytes.
